*** TinyURL ***


Creating a short hash or identifier for a service like TinyURL with 7 characters involves several considerations. Here's an approach you could take:

Character Set: First, decide on your character set. A common choice is to use:

Lowercase letters (a-z): 26 characters
Uppercase letters (A-Z): 26 characters
Numbers (0-9): 10 characters This gives a total of 62 possible characters.
Possible Combinations: With 7 characters and 62 possible characters for each position, you have: 62^7 = 3,521,614,606,208 possible unique combinations

Generation Method: There are several ways to generate the 7-character hash:

a) Random Generation:

Generate 7 random characters from your character set.
Check if it already exists in your database. If it does, generate a new one.

b) Base62 Encoding:

Assign an incrementing number to each URL.
Convert this number to base 62 using your character set.
Pad the result to 7 characters if needed.

c) Hash and Truncate:

Hash the original URL using a cryptographic hash function (e.g., SHA-256).
SHA-256 , means 256 bits --> 32 bytes --> 64 character hexadecimal (A-F 0-9)
Take the first 7 characters of the hash.
If there's a collision, rehash or use a different portion of the hash.


